+## 8. The command bar *is* the sign-in surface when unsigned
+
+Unsigned visitors type their email into the hero command bar and hit Send —
+that is the natural affordance on mobile. Hiding magic-link sign-in behind a
+cryptic "E" avatar produced the exact failure mode: email in the ask field,
+then the red "Sign in as the owner to use the command bar." banner.
+
+Unsigned: the bar is `type="email"` + **Send link**. Signed-in: it becomes the
+ask field. Chips nudge toward sign-in instead of stuffing a question into a
+disabled ask path.
+
+## 9. The sb_publishable_* fallback was unregistered
+
+`sb_publishable_obr-7Y0u02p5c5pD-5f3Sw_zda5lWTa` returns HTTP 401
+"Unregistered API key" against `pkydkbuodikttfeawqsw` for both Auth and
+PostgREST. The working publishable credential is the project's legacy JWT anon
+key (already shipped in the Vercel bundle via `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`).
+Do not reinstate the unregistered sb_publishable string as a source fallback.
+
+## 10. flock-ask is Merged, not Deployed
+
+```
+$ curl -sS -X POST "$SUPABASE_URL/functions/v1/flock-ask" ...
+{"code":"NOT_FOUND","message":"Requested function was not found"}
+```
+
+Even a perfect owner session cannot ask the flock until the Edge Function is
+deployed and its secrets are set (checklist step 4). The client now surfaces
+that 404 as an honest message instead of a generic failure.
+
+---
